==English==

===Etymology===
Borrowed from {{bor|en|grc|σκληρός||hard}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈsklɛəɹə/|/ˈsklɪəɹə/}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɛəɹə|ɪəɹə|s=2}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|s|sclerae|scleræ}}

# {{lb|en|anatomy}} The white of the [[eye]]; the tough outer coat of the eye that covers the [[eyeball]] except for the [[cornea]].
#: {{syn|en|sclerotic|sclerotic coat}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2007|author=Junot Diaz|title=The Brief Wondrous Life of Oscar Wao|passage=She'd been back a week and it was clear that college-level track was kicking her ass, the '''sclera''' in her normally wide manga-eyes were shot through with blood vessels.}}

